The first term is a [[Definition:Riemann Sum|Riemann sum]] for $-\displaystyle \int p \log p$.

Properties linear in $p$ survive the limit, but non-negativity does not.
For example, if $X$ is [[Definition:Continuous Uniform Distribution|uniform]] on $\closedint 0 {\frac 1 2}$ then $\map h X = -\log 2 < 0$.
{{qed}}
